# Each loop is built twice: the dead zones of the constants are asked in front, `at` goes round as a number. The typed build was walked as if its turns were quiet, so at the first mark the turn began again in the other copy, and every later turn of the scan ran there, with `at` in a box.
# The purchase is kept and its typed build is left at a call on the usual way: the builds are made again, the typed one under all that the loop does. Both calls stand in it as well as in the other copy.
# RUN(CALLS): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# CALLS-COUNT-2: = CallDirect {{*}} function=f1
# CALLS-NOT: = CallDirect {{*}} function=f1
# RUN(ODD): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# ODD-COUNT-2: = CallDirect {{*}} function=f2
# ODD-NOT: = CallDirect {{*}} function=f2
# The start of pastGroup arrives as a number. It is asked for an int32 in front of the loop though two ways round bring what a call gives: those ways are asked where they come round, and `at` goes round as an int32.
# RUN(START): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# START: i32 @Int32) isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true
# In countMarks the other copy is closed and `at` starts as an integer. What a call gives comes round as a number or a text, or as anything: it is asked for an int32 on that edge, and the head of the typed build keeps `at` as an int32; what fails goes to the head of the other copy, which takes the turn.
# RUN(ASKED): walk f4 mechanisms=all
# ASKED: frequency=Rare isLoopHead=true
# ASKED: = CallDirect {{*}} function=f1
# ASKED: = CallDirect {{*}} function=f2
# ASKED: i32 @Int32) isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true
# ASKED: = CallDirect {{*}} function=f1
# ASKED: = TypeTest {{*}} testedType=i32
# ASKED: = CallDirect {{*}} function=f2
# ASKED: = TypeTest {{*}} testedType=i32
# The helper gives texts, fractions, numbers past every int32, NaN, an object, -0, nothing and a big integer; its other code lays another value into a variable that every turn reads, and throws; the scan starts at what is no int32 and no number; the text is no text.
